<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harburg-Wilhelmsburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1927–1937</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harburg-Wilhelmsburg was a Prussian city on the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, formed in 1927 by merging the industrial towns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harburg-hamburg">Harburg</a> and Wilhelmsburg. A centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rubber">rubber</a>, oil and port industries, it was incorporated into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-hamburg-act">Greater Hamburg Act</a> of 1937, and its two parts are now Hamburg districts.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harburg-wilhelmsburg.jpg" alt="Harburg-Wilhelmsburg" width="320" height="156" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Staro1 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamburg-Harburg_Rathaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
